      "group": "g-region",
      "accept": [
        "aws-cognito"
      ],
      "near_miss": "aws-iam",
      "hint_cue": "con su cuenta de Google",
      "explanation": "Un grupo de usuarios de Cognito agrega el botón de Google, hace el intercambio OAuth 2.0 y OIDC, y le da a la app tokens de ID y de acceso que caducan (de 5 minutos a 1 día) y un token de actualización para pedir otros.",
      "refs": [
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/cognito-user-pools-social-idp.html",
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/amazon-cognito-user-pools-using-the-id-token.html",
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/amazon-cognito-user-pools-using-the-refresh-token.html",
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/introduction.html",
        "https://aws.amazon.com/compare/cognito-and-iam/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "number": 2,
      "cell": {
        "c": 2.5,
        "r": 1.5
      },
      "group": "g-region",
      "accept": [
        "aws-api-gateway"
      ],
      "near_miss": "aws-nlb",
      "hint_cue": "token inválido, caducado o de otro emisor",
      "explanation": "Con un autorizador JWT en la ruta, API Gateway revisa la firma, el emisor (iss), la audiencia y la caducidad (exp) y niega la solicitud si algo falla. Llega a la subred privada con una integración privada: un VPC link hacia un balanceador o Cloud Map.",
      "refs": [
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/http-api-jwt-authorizer.html",
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/network/introduction.html",
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/http-api-develop-integrations-private.html"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "number": 3,
      "cell": {
        "c": 6.75,
        "r": 0.5
      },
      "group": "g-region",
      "accept": [
        "aws-kms"
      ],
      "near_miss": "aws-secrets-manager",
      "hint_cue": "llaves de la empresa que rotan cada año",
      "explanation": "Una llave de KMS administrada por el cliente puede rotar sola, cada 365 días si no se indica otro periodo, y CloudTrail registra cada operación criptográfica con ella, como Decrypt o GenerateDataKey.",
      "refs": [
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/help-panel/kms/latest/console/hp-automatic-key-rotation.html",
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/logging-using-cloudtrail.html",
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/intro.html",
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/security-encryption.html"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "number": 4,
      "cell": {
        "c": 6.75,
        "r": 2.3
      },
      "group": "g-region",
      "accept": [
        "aws-guardduty"
      ],
      "near_miss": "aws-inspector",
      "hint_cue": "IP sospechosa",
      "explanation": "GuardDuty analiza los eventos de CloudTrail, los VPC Flow Logs y las consultas DNS; su hallazgo MaliciousIPCaller avisa cuando alguien invoca una API de AWS desde una IP maliciosa conocida.",
      "refs": [
        "https://aws.amazon.com/guardduty/pricing/",
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_finding-types-iam.html",
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/what-is-inspector.html"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "number": 5,
      "cell": {
        "c": 6.75,
        "r": 3.6
      },
      "group": "g-region",
      "accept": [
        "aws-cloudtrail"
      ],
      "near_miss": "aws-vpc-flow-logs",
      "hint_cue": "quién cambió una regla de firewall",
      "explanation": "Cada evento de CloudTrail guarda quién hizo la solicitud (userIdentity), cuándo (eventTime) y desde qué IP (sourceIPAddress), y CloudTrail deja ver la creación, el cambio y el borrado de recursos.",
      "refs": [
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/logging-monitoring-for-application-owners/cloudtrail.html",
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-event-reference-record-contents.html",
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/flow-logs.html"
      ]
    }
